If a clinician identifies an opioid-use-disorder in a patient then the clinician may initiate an opioid-use-disorder-intervention for the patient.
Every opioid-use-disorder-intervention can possibly save a life.
If a clinician identifies an opioid-use-disorder in a patient then the clinician should conduct a patient-safety-collaboration with the patient for a successful-treatment-likelihood-increase.
Every patient-safety-collaboration can increase a successful-treatment-likelihood.
